        ColorLoader.matugenColors.on_surface :
        ColorLoader.pywalColors.special?.foreground || "#e1e2e8"

    // ...existing code...
}
````

## Method 5: Create Auto-Update Script

Create a script to automatically update QuickShell colors when wallpaper changes:

````bash
#!/bin/bash

# Update pywal colors
wal -i "$1" -n

# Copy colors to quickshell
cp ~/.cache/wal/colors.json ~/.config/quickshell/pywal_colors.json

# If using matugen
if command -v matugen &> /dev/null; then
